","closed_at":"2026-04-28T14:14:30Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118948","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948.patch","merged_at":"2026-04-28T14:14:30Z"},"body":"Fixes #118923.\r\n\r\nIt seems the conversion of Godot's `Plane` to Jolt's `JPH::Plane`, and `WorldBoundaryShape3D` as a result, was incorrectly implemented by me, as Godot expresses its planes as:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/6d6e822c689acb54bf86e19cc2bbbe3fa567b123/doc/classes/Plane.xml#L154-L157\r\n\r\n... whereas Jolt expresses it as:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/6d6e822c689acb54bf86e19cc2bbbe3fa567b123/thirdparty/jolt_physics/Jolt/Geometry/Plane.h#L9-L10\r\n\r\n... resulting in the plane distance effectively being negated when using Jolt.\r\n\r\nThis fixes that by negating said negation, which is a breaking change.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.co